# Citation metadata for the COMPASS software (Citation File Format 1.2.0). GitHub reads this
# file for its "Cite this repository" box. The DOI of the release will be added here when the
# Zenodo archive of the release exists. The license has no SPDX identifier, so it is given as a
# URL. (ORCID: to be added by the author.)
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use COMPASS in your work, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "COMPASS: statistically verified refinement of probabilistic programs"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
authors:
  - family-names: Gabitto
    given-names: Mariano
    affiliation: Allen Institute
repository-code: "https://github.com/M-Lab-Repo/compass"
url: "https://github.com/M-Lab-Repo/compass"
abstract: >-
  COMPASS refines Bayesian models written as NumPyro programs. Language-model agents diagnose
  the model, search the statistical literature and propose candidate refinements; a
  deterministic verifier with no language model in it fits the baseline and the candidate with
  MCMC and accepts a refinement only when a fixed statistical rule is met.
keywords:
  - bayesian-statistics
  - probabilistic-programming
  - numpyro
  - model-criticism
  - cross-validation
  - mcmc
  - llm-agents
license-url: "https://github.com/M-Lab-Repo/compass/blob/main/LICENSE.txt"
